{"title": "Devils Hole: Floods and Earthquake-Triggered Mini-Tsunamis", "description": "Last month, moonsoonal rains triggered a flash flood at Devils Hole, home to rare pupfishes and part of Death Valley National Park located within Ash Meadows National Wildlife Refuge. Just two days later, an earthquake thousands of miles away in Alaska caused a mini tsunami (called a seiche) at Devils Hole. While events like these are common, scientists with the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service, National Park Service, and U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) continue to learn more about how these fascinating disturbances play an important role within the system. \n\nAn audio described version can be found on our website: https://www.nps.gov/media/video/view.htm?id=1C1D516B-B49C-474E-83D6-0A4B9CAC5479\n\nVideo Credit: USGS/P. Pearsall", "uploader": "Death Valley National Park", "uploader_id": "100064756474257", "thumbnail": "https://scontent-dfw5-2.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t15.5256-10/240826485_267520085198488_8899533944499390986_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx1920x1080&ctp=s960x960&_nc_cat=104&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=50ce42&_nc_ohc=6zD-V6mHwEkQ7kNvwGfO55g&_nc_oc=AdqvIJaGqVjpA7dZ518b1whO7QeNwn7ki8JxF3Z7VJS1u8Yes7hCjQR2YH6G_7QBc4s&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-2.xx&_nc_gid=q1qJ3IoneNiHbUU6-Wxlcw&_nc_ss=70289&oh=00_AQSSe6gYRFp8fGTi1UthA726Fpa5jwV98Stfpuf6tWfOrw&oe=6AF0AFA8", "view_count": 5243, "concurrent_view_count": 0, "duration": 163.264, "id": "267518495198647", "formats": [{"format_id": "1018999902505546a", "manifest_url": "https://www.facebook.com/dash_mpd_debug.mpd?v=267518495198647&dummy=.mpd", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 49.348, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://video-dfw6-2.xx.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m412/AQN6js4lYDrWYNpy6ozuJhwZsTWUH9-MXsRArk9tMDehUZXiBRFhPKdteR1h7AhqUEpkBqWgwNng6KfFvHQmVL3G.mp4?_nc_cat=108&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=video-dfw6-2.xx.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=O1vIN95Bo-8Q7kNvwGueSNr&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=q1qJ3IoneNiHbUU